 FILE ASSEMBLY, VERIFICATION AND VALIDATION                       2525 1451
 Coordinator: A. Trkov                                            2525 1451
                                                                  2525 1451
 The file integrity and internal consistency with respect         2525 1451
 to format requirements was checked with the ENDF Utility         2525 1451
 codes and ENDF Pre-Processing codes. Processability was          2525 1451
 checked by generating and ACE file for Monte Carlo               2525 1451
 calculations and a multigroup file in MATXS format for           2525 1451
 deterministic calculations. The plots produced by the heatr      2525 1451
 and acer modules of NJOY were inspected. Comparison plots        2525 1451
 were made with ENDF/B-VII.0 data. Furthermore, comparison        2525 1451
 plots with the ENDVER package were made against selected         2525 1451
 experimental data from the EXFOR database.                       2525 1451
                                                                  2525 1451
 Integral validation was performed by comparing the thermal       2525 1451
 capture cross section Sig0 and ratio Q0 of the resonance         2525 1451
 integrals and the thermal cross section values from the          2525 1451
 IUPAC database for neutron activation analysis                   2525 1451
        IUPAC       This work   ENDF/B-VII.0                      2525 1451
 Sig0   13.19-+0.6% 13.27-+1.1% 13.42                             2525 1451
 Q0     1.053-+3.0% 0.998-+3.6% 0.867                             2525 1451
                                                                  2525 1451
 More extensive testing of the cross sections in the resonance    2525 1451
 region was done by modelling the Grenoble lead-slowing-down      2525 1451
 benchmark (Perrot et al. NSE 144, 2003, p.p.142-156), which      2525 1451
 showed excellent agreement of the calculated capture reaction    2525 1451
 rate with the measurement. The results explain the improvement   2525 1451
 in the Q0 value stated in the previous paragraph.                2525 1451
                                                                  2525 1451
 Cross sections in the fast energy range were probed by           2525 1451
 modelling the Oktavian benchmark from the SINBAD database, in    2525 1451
 which the leakage spectrum from a manganese sphere with a 14-MeV 2525 1451
 D-T source was measured. The results confirm good performance of 2525 1451
 the data, which is at least as good as any competing evaluation. 2525 1451
                                                                  2525 1451
 Detailed results will be presented in a separate report.         2525 1451
                                                                  2525 1451
 FAST ENERGY REGION                                               2525 1451
 Authors: R. Capote, E. Soukhovitskii, A. Trkov,                  2525 1451
          A. Milocco, M. Herman                                   2525 1451
                                                                  2525 1451
 CROSS-SECTION EVALUATION PROCEDURE                               2525 1451
                                                                  2525 1451
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                2525 1451
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               2525 1451
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             2525 1451
                                                                  2525 1451
 Available experimental data were interpreted  using              2525 1451
 nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-3 by M. Herman                2525 1451
 et al [EMP]. This code integrates into a single                  2525 1451
 system a number of important modules and features:               2525 1451
                                                                  2525 1451
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 2525 1451
   coupled-channels (ECIS06 by J. Raynal)                         2525 1451
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    2525 1451
   HRTW width fluctuation correction                              2525 1451
 - Quantum-mechanical MSD TUL model (codes ORION &                2525 1451
   TRISTAN by H. Lenske), and MSC NVWY model                      2525 1451
 - Exciton model with angular momentum coupling                   2525 1451
   (code DEGAS by E. Betak and P. Oblozinsky) that                2525 1451
   represents a good approximation to the DSD model               2525 1451
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      2525 1451
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 2525 1451
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                2525 1451
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   2525 1451
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                2525 1451
   discrete transitions                                           2525 1451
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL library [RIPL]                2525 1451
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                2525 1451
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               2525 1451
   and gamma strength functions based on the RIPL                 2525 1451
   library [RIPL]                                                 2525 1451
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              2525 1451
   EXFOR/CSISRS library                                           2525 1451
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A. Trkov)                    2525 1451
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 2525 1451
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                2525 1451
   PrePro codes by R. Cullen                                      2525 1451
 - Checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                        2525 1451
 - Support for NJOY                                               2525 1451
                                                                  2525 1451
 PARAMETERIZATIONS                                                2525 1451
                                                                  2525 1451
 Following models and parameters were used in the                 2525 1451
 current evaluation:                                              2525 1451
                                                                  2525 1451
 Discrete levels were taken from the RIPL-3 level                 2525 1451
 file, based on the 2007 version of ENSDF.                        2525 1451
 ENDF formatting enabled                                          2525 1451
 Exclusive spectra available up to emission loop #  1             2525 1451
 Coupled Channels (ECIS) used for direct inelastic scattering     2525 1451
 Exciton model calculations with code PCROSS                      2525 1451
 Cluster emission in terms of the Iwamoto-Harada model            2525 1451
 Kalbach systematics angular distributions (see RIPL-1)           2525 1451
 Mean free path parameter in PCROSS set to  1.2 (Recommended ~ 1.52525 1451
 Max hole number in PCROSS set to 0.50*sqrt(g*U)                  2525 1451
    being U the CN excitation energy                              2525 1451
 Width fluctuations calculated within HRTW  up to 4.00 MeV        2525 1451
 EMPIRE-specific level densities                                  2525 1451
 Emission width of ejectile 0 from  56Mn multiplied by   1.120    2525 1451
 PE emission width of ejectile 0 from  56Mn multiplied by  6.000  2525 1451
 Fusion cross section was scaled by factor  0.975                 2525 1451
 E1 strength function set to MLO1                                 2525 1451
 GDR parameters from RIPL-2/Exp.data+Plujko systematics           2525 1451
                                                                  2525 1451
